<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:13Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:40af4db108b6b605271dff8f8ab94167e7908876d3c506bd7a99ab94b58262e5</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:42:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why Indian nationals are still ending up in Russia's war on Ukraine</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2d469e48ca736ac1ed8265fdcff693230b6afffa23fc91017a935230da5b890f</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:43:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T13:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-indian-nationals-are-still-ending-up-in-russia-s-war-on-ukraine/a-80048537--f2a88cb80a6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-indian-nationals-are-still-ending-up-in-russia-s-war-on-ukraine/a-80048537?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Whether through deception or desperation, Indians continue to be drawn into Russia's war in Ukraine. What can New Delhi do to protect its citizens from ending up fighting in Ukraine?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>In Afghanistan, no female doctor often means no treatment for women</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c2a6bba83f55f455cf5e3cb068f3b8aa83109be4d5de6ae806df2f441f482b1</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/in-afghanistan-no-female-doctor-often-means-no-treatment-for-women/a-80047053--cac71a2a15bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/in-afghanistan-no-female-doctor-often-means-no-treatment-for-women/a-80047053?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Millions of women in Afghanistan, particularly pregnant women, are suffering under Taliban restrictions and are increasingly losing access to life-saving medical care.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: Deepfakes and 'US abandons Taiwan' claims spread ahead of vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dca7a28323a79f094d5b890e19a58292a0e4b5475acf751f8df0fa5c5a48d108</id><updated>2026-11-25T18:44:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-25T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-deepfakes-and-us-abandons-taiwan-claims-spread-ahead-of-vote/a-80004834--56b12ab42141.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-deepfakes-and-us-abandons-taiwan-claims-spread-ahead-of-vote/a-80004834?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ahead of local elections, Taiwan is seeing a surge in AI-generated attacks on mayoral candidate Puma Shen, alongside disinformation portraying the US as abandoning the island.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine's bid for NATO membership and more air defense remains controversial</title><id>urn:rssync: